Let jumps be a list of 2, 3, 1, 1, and 4.
Let last be the last position of jumps.
Let steps be 0.
Let start be 0.
Let current end be 0.
Let farthest be 0.
Repeat while current end is less than last.
For every scan from start to current end, let reach be scan plus item scan of jumps, if reach is greater than farthest, set farthest to reach.
Set start to one more than current end.
Set current end to farthest.
Add 1 to steps.

Print steps.
